.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-list - List temporary previews


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List previews: ID, access, target and state. Only active previews are shown by default;
--all adds previews that ended in the last 30 days, and --state picks one state. Filter with
--q and --owner; page with --cursor and --limit (1-200, default 100). Use a preview's ID with
status, inspect, replay, stop or delete.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	include ended previews (kept 30 days after they end)

.PP
\fB--cursor\fP=""
	continue a previous page

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical preview resources as JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=100
	maximum results (1-200)

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb preview list
  pb preview list --all
  pb preview list --state active --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
